<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20273] orr_offset using dst instead of src in endian helpers</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20273</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="code panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="codeContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre class="code-java"&gt;
&lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;static&lt;/span&gt; inline void orr_cpu_to_le(struct out_read_reply *orr_dst,
                 &lt;span class="code-keyword"&gt;const&lt;/span&gt; struct out_read_reply *orr_src){
    orr_dst-&amp;gt;orr_size = cpu_to_le32(orr_src-&amp;gt;orr_size);
    orr_dst-&amp;gt;orr_padding = cpu_to_le32(orr_src-&amp;gt;orr_padding);
    orr_dst-&amp;gt;orr_offset = cpu_to_le64(orr_dst-&amp;gt;orr_offset); &lt;span class="code-comment"&gt;//cpu_to_le64(orr_src-&amp;gt;orr_offset)
&lt;/span&gt;} &lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Currently this is only called in-place (orr_cpu_to_le(orr, orr)), so no bug is triggered today. However, anyone refactoring or extending the code who calls these helpers with distinct src and dst pointers will get a silent misbehavior, as orr_offset will never be copied from the source.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Discovered by code inspect.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
